{"id": "EUVD-2026-107249", "enisaUuid": "0506e79e-9ad7-3520-96fe-e5eca1f3c169", "description": "Trudesk through 1.2.11 contains a path traversal and authorization bypass vulnerability in accountsController.uploadImage that allows authenticated users to overwrite other users' avatars via form-supplied _id and username fields. Attackers can supply a username like /../../../x to bypass the incomplete CVE-2022-1752 sanitization and write png, jpg, jpeg, or gif files outside public/uploads/users.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T12:39:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:39:54", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@leediay/multiple-vuln-trudesk-1211", "https://github.com/polonel/trudesk/blob/v1.2.11/src/controllers/accounts.js#L454-L553", "https://github.com/polonel/trudesk", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/trudesk-through-1.2.11-path-traversal-and-authorization-bypass-via-profile-image-upload"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-114402", "GHSA-2xw4-xqvw-cxg5"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.31, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3038414a-5b05-3cce-b460-c82753d0e8c6", "product": {"name": "trudesk", "vendor": {"name": "polonel"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.2.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "efa25a43-2ad7-38a1-b5a5-458c546e1895", "vendor": {"name": "polonel"}}], "isExploited": false}